          "guid": "ms5ubmg896xq118y",
          "message": {
            "text": "Holding restartTerminal open on a caller-controlled deferred is what makes this testable at all — the real in-flight window is however long one HTTP call takes, so a timing-based test would be flaky in exactly the direction that hides the bug.\n\nVerified the tests fail against the pre-fix code (guard removed, target read from the captured parameter):\n\n× runs ONE spawn and opens ONLY the dedicated view\n× collapses repeated clicks during one in-flight spawn into a single spawn\n  Tests  2 failed | 3 passed (5)\n\nThe discrimination is the useful part: the two race cases fail, and the three control cases — plain single click still centers, the guard releases for a later spawn, a failed spawn enlarges nothing — still pass. So the suite is pinning the race specifically, not just \"something changed in this file\".\n\nThe tile is exited rather than not_spawned deliberately; see the note on spawnAndEnlarge in src/client/terminalTileGridCenter.tsx for why only that path can be re-entered.\n\nThe e2e half (e2e/dashboard-cold-tile-dblclick.spec.ts) covers what a unit test cannot: real click/dblclick dispatch through the browser's own event ordering, with the restart route delayed 1.2 s. Its load-bearing assertion is the restart COUNT (2 pre-fix, 1 post-fix) — the view-state assertions passed even pre-fix in one run, since which overlay survives depends on the order the two spawns settle.\n",
            "markdown": "Holding `restartTerminal` open on a caller-controlled deferred is what makes this testable at all — the real in-flight window is however long one HTTP call takes, so a timing-based test would be flaky in exactly the direction that hides the bug.\n\nVerified the tests fail against the pre-fix code (guard removed, target read from the captured parameter):\n\n```\n× runs ONE spawn and opens ONLY the dedicated view\n× collapses repeated clicks during one in-flight spawn into a single spawn\n  Tests  2 failed | 3 passed (5)\n```\n\nThe discrimination is the useful part: the two race cases fail, and the three control cases — plain single click still centers, the guard releases for a later spawn, a failed spawn enlarges nothing — still pass. So the suite is pinning the race specifically, not just \"something changed in this file\".\n\nThe tile is `exited` rather than `not_spawned` deliberately; see the note on `spawnAndEnlarge` in `src/client/terminalTileGridCenter.tsx` for why only that path can be re-entered.\n\nThe e2e half (`e2e/dashboard-cold-tile-dblclick.spec.ts`) covers what a unit test cannot: real click/dblclick dispatch through the browser's own event ordering, with the restart route delayed 1.2 s. Its load-bearing assertion is the restart COUNT (2 pre-fix, 1 post-fix) — the view-state assertions passed even pre-fix in one run, since which overlay survives depends on the order the two spawns settle.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/client/terminalTileGridSpawnRace.test.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 15,
                  "endLine": 25,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": " * These tests hold `restartTerminal` open on a controllable deferred, which is\n * the only way to make the in-flight window wide enough to drive\n * deterministically — the real window is however long the HTTP call takes, so a\n * timing-based test would be inherently flaky.\n *\n * The tile is `exited` rather than `not_spawned` deliberately: only the exited\n * path awaits anything, so it is the only one that can be re-entered. A\n * `not_spawned` tile runs `spawnAndEnlarge` straight through with no await and\n * is already `alive` by the time `dblclick` arrives.\n */\nimport { afterEach, beforeEach, describe, expect, it, vi } from 'vitest';"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "tags": [
              "test-evidence"
            ]
          },
